The Switch
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/foundry]

FIXME(dread): His hand rests on the control. "Press it, or stop me. Now." The plant is already labouring under him, the brakes off, the needles beginning to climb.
FIXME(dread): To stop him is to kill him, and that is not the simple thing it looks. A man the deal made deathless does not fall to ordinary steel, though the PC has no way to know it until they try.

choices:

* Run him through with the shimmering blade = Use the edge he gave you [requires has shimmering_blade]
    FIXME(action): The Color-tempered blade does the work cleanly; a thing built to part steel plate does not strain at a man. Only now does the reason he pressed it into the PC's hands arrive. The plant is already running away, and his death does not call it back. The PC walks out ahead of the smoke, the blade still in hand.
    +add_level
    +finish_dungeon

* Draw your own weapon on him = Stop him by force
    FIXME(action): The PC strikes with whatever they carry. The blow lands and does nothing. He looks at the PC, almost sorry, his hand never leaving the control. Ordinary steel is nothing to him. Then he throws the switch himself. There is time, and the PC walks out ahead of the smoke while the plant begins to come apart behind them.
    +add_level
    +finish_dungeon

* Step back and let him finish = Give him the moment
    FIXME(dread): The PC stands away. Suhail throws the control, and the plant begins to labour toward its end. They walk out together at a steady pace, ahead of the smoke.
    FIXME(mundane): On the road away from the site, a party of engineers is heading toward it. They heard the blast. They ask, with professional interest, whether the structure came down cleanly.
    +add_level
    +finish_dungeon
